    apply: "Write a blessing for each of your children and read it to them or keep it for the right moment. Give each child a growing responsibility this month. If your children are adults, ask them how you can support them and listen. Pray for them by name.",
    activity: "Read Psalm 127:4-5 and 3 John 4 and discuss the picture of arrows. Ask learners to list the skills and values they want children to have before leaving home. Practise composing a blessing. Pray together for children and parents.",
    takeHome: "Read Psalm 127, Genesis 2:18-25, Luke 2:41-52 and 3 John. Write a blessing for your children. Memorise 3 John 4.",
    prayer: "Thank God for the privilege of raising children. Ask for grace to release them. Pray for children entering adulthood.",
    teacher: "Remind learners that the final examination is next week. Be gentle with those who are grieving over children, or who have no children. Affirm that spiritual parenting is open to all. Encourage learners to keep growing as parents.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners what the aim of parenting is and how to release children.",
    mcq1: ["What is the picture in Psalm 127:4?", ["Children as arrows in the hand of a warrior", "Children as stones", "Children as coins", "Children as trees"], 0, "Arrows to be released."],
